00:38:54.370 --> 00:39:01.330
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Never met her in-laws because Israeli restrictions make it very hard to travel between the West Bank and Gaza.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>因为以色列的限制使约旦河西岸和加沙之间的旅行变得非常困难，所以她从未见过姻亲。

00:39:01.330 --> 00:39:15.420
<v Bushra Khalidi>Like, how is it that this has to happen for us to meet and for my son to meet his grandparents for the first time, you know? Like, how? Why? Why do we have to go through this?
<v Bushra Khalidi>我的意思是，为什么非得发生这种情况，我们才能见面，我的儿子才能第一次见到他的祖父母，你知道吗？怎么会这样？为什么？为什么我们非得经历这些？

00:39:15.420 --> 00:39:24.090
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>What is it going to mean to your family to have spent this money on this, like long-term or--
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>你们全家在这件事上花了这笔钱，从长远来看意味着什么，或者——

00:39:24.090 --> 00:39:27.160
<v Bushra Khalidi>Shame. Shame.
<v Bushra Khalidi>羞耻。羞耻。

00:39:27.160 --> 00:39:30.760
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Shame? Why?
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>羞耻？为什么？

00:39:30.760 --> 00:39:42.050
<v Bushra Khalidi>Because they're ashamed. Because that's not who we are, you know? We've been rendered destitute, you know? They're not destitute people, you know? They had a beautiful home and beautiful lives.
<v Bushra Khalidi>因为他们感到羞耻。因为那不是我们的本性，你知道吗？我们变得一贫如洗，你知道吗？他们不是赤贫的人，你知道吗？他们曾经有过漂亮的房子和美好的生活。

00:39:42.050 --> 00:40:13.220
<v Bushra Khalidi>And to put that on your son, I mean, I don't know. I don't know if it's shame, but it's like guilt maybe. It's like they're so grateful that they're ashamed to say it. You know what I mean? It's embarrassing that they put that on us. And so we don't talk about it. It's not like there's a thank you because even a thank you is not enough for them. And so it's better not to say it.
<v Bushra Khalidi>把这个负担压在我的儿子身上，我的意思是，我不知道。我不知道是不是羞耻，但更像是内疚。他们非常感激，以至于羞于说出口。你明白我的意思吗？他们让我们背负这些，这很尴尬。所以我们不谈论它。并不是说连个“谢谢”都没有，因为即使是谢谢对他们来说也不够。所以最好什么都不说。

00:40:13.220 --> 00:40:16.400
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Do you want to talk about it?
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>你想谈谈它吗？

00:40:16.400 --> 00:40:42.310
<v Bushra Khalidi>Um, no, because I would do it a million times over again. And they know that. I just need to know that they're alive and that they're good. And now, I mean, the thing is, is that they're in Egypt now, and I'm in Egypt now. And but the road ahead is so hard. And coming here and just seeing them, they're not the same people. They never will be the same people, you know?
<v Bushra Khalidi>嗯，不，因为我会再做一百万次同样的事。他们也知道这一点。我只需要知道他们还活着，他们很好。现在，问题是他们已经在埃及了，我也在埃及。但前方的路太艰难了。来到这里看到他们，他们已经不再是以前的人了。他们永远不会再是以前的自己了，你知道吗？

00:40:42.310 --> 00:41:29.730
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>This brings us back to Yousef. Yousef, who knew this, he knew leaving Gaza meant he would not be the same person. And still, Yousef was going through all these steps through a system designed to frustrate, deter, and bankrupt him. Yousef's version of this process, raising an astounding amount of money, getting the cash in dollars physically to the Hala office, Yousef's maneuvers were not the exact same as Bushra's, but they were just as involved and absurd, right up until he was registered and waiting for permission to do something he did not want to do.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>这又回到了尤瑟夫身上。尤瑟夫知道这一点，他知道离开加沙意味着他将不再是原来的那个人。然而，尤瑟夫依然走过了所有程序，走过了一套旨在挫败、威慑并让他破产的系统。尤瑟夫处理这个过程的方式——筹集巨额资金、亲自将美元现金送到哈拉办公室——尤瑟夫的做法虽然和布什拉的不完全一样，但同样错综复杂且荒谬，直到他注册完毕，等待许可去完成他其实并不想做的事。

00:41:29.730 --> 00:41:51.590
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>When he was growing up, Yousef's uncle used to tell him he reminded him of his grandfather. He grew up hearing this a lot, the similarities to his grandfather. And Yousef got it. His grandfather hustled, made things happen. He was resourceful. But Yousef has been thinking about this lately, what it meant to be like his grandfather, what else it meant.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>尤瑟夫成长过程中，他叔叔常说他很像他的祖父。他从小就经常听到这个，说他和祖父很像。尤瑟夫也理解。他的祖父很努力，能把事情办成。他足智多谋。但尤瑟夫最近一直在思考，像他祖父意味着什么，还有什么别的含义。

00:41:51.590 --> 00:42:17.380
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>His grandfather is the one who got everyone to Jabalia, to the refugee camp in the north of Gaza, when they were all pushed out of their homes in what is now Israel in 1948. His grandfather is the one who made sure everyone got set up in the same place next to each other, made sure they survived, had housing, had their needs met. He made sure they were safe, and they were together. And they were.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>他的祖父是那个在1948年他们都被赶出现在的以色列家园时，把大家带到加沙北部贾巴利亚难民营的人。他的祖父是那个确保每个人都住在一起、确保他们幸存下来、有住房、需求得到满足的人。他确保了大家的安全和团聚。他们确实做到了。

00:42:17.380 --> 00:42:39.090
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Jabalia Camp became a small city. People moved to bigger apartments nearby, had kids, but the family stayed safe and right next to each other. 75 years later, Yousef was the one who moved his sisters and their families to a tent camp in Rafah so they could all be nearby, safe and together.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>贾巴利亚难民营变成了一座小城市。人们搬到了附近更大的公寓，有了孩子，但家人始终平安且住在一起。75年后，尤瑟夫是那个把他的姐妹和她们的家庭带到拉法帐篷营地的人，这样他们就能在一起，平安且团聚。

00:42:39.090 --> 00:42:58.130
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>They were there for three months when Yousef heard from a contact in Egypt, a friend with connections at the Hala Company, who told him that his family's names were likely to be listed in the next week. He wasn't just failing at keeping the family together. He was the one who was going to split them up.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>他们在那里待了三个月，尤瑟夫从埃及的一位联系人那里得到消息，那是位在哈拉公司有关系的朋友，他告诉尤瑟夫，他家人的名字很可能会在下周出现在名单上。他不只是未能让家人团聚，他竟然是那个要拆散他们的人。

