<v Yousef Hammash>[LAUGHS] I have two jeans pants, two T-shirts, two jackets, and actually, most of it, I will leave it for my brothers-in-law. I'm just going to take just what I could wear during the first day and just a pajama for the next day. And that's it. The easiest part is packing. [LAUGHS]
<v Yousef Hammash>[笑声] 我有两条牛仔裤，两件T恤，两件夹克，实际上，大部分东西我会留给我姐夫。我只带上第一天能穿的，再加一件换洗的睡衣。就这样。打包是最简单的。[笑声]

00:43:37.870 --> 00:43:41.530
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>What's the hardest part?
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>最难的部分是什么？

00:43:41.530 --> 00:44:13.310
<v Yousef Hammash>[SIGHS] It's also packing. [LAUGHS] Tangibly, there is nothing to be packed during the journey, but we are packing our relations with our families now. I don't know how it's going to be that day when we are just going out. And I don't want to really think about that moment because I don't know how it's going to be. And, yeah. Yeah, it's going to be difficult. I don't want to think about it. Let's wait and see.
<v Yousef Hammash>[叹气] 也是打包。[笑声] 从有形上看，旅途中没什么可打包的，但我们现在正在打包我们与家人的关系。我不知道我们要离开的那一天会是什么样子。我真的不想去想那一刻，因为我不知道会怎么样。是的。是的，这会很困难。我不想去想它。让我们走着瞧吧。

