00:45:28.160 --> 00:45:48.990
<v Yousef Hammash>So I decided we were having iftar with my sisters. I told them that we are leaving the day after. And I just wanted to use that day with them. We agreed to have iftar together, all of us. And we were planning for tomorrow that even I don't want to go to work. I want to spend it with my sisters. I take my family there. We spend the entire day there.
<v Yousef Hammash>所以我决定……我们当时正和姐妹们开斋。我告诉她们我们后天就要走了。我只想利用那一天和她们在一起。我们商定大家一起开斋。我们计划明天甚至不去工作。我想和我的姐妹们在一起。我把家人带到那里。我们在那里待了一整天。

00:45:48.990 --> 00:46:14.270
<v Yousef Hammash>Then we go back to prepare ourself to travel. And suddenly, when we were there, one of-- it's the wife of one of our colleagues who lives with us. She called and she said, your names are listed. And it was very shocking, and suddenly, everything became a chaos. Everyone started crying. And it was a very emotional moment that I didn't want to see.
<v Yousef Hammash>然后我们回去准备出发。突然，当我们还在那里时，我们的一位同事的妻子，她和我们住在一起，她打来电话说，你们的名字上名单了。这太令人震惊了，突然间，一切都陷入了混乱。每个人都开始哭泣。那是一个非常情绪化的时刻，我不想看到。

00:46:14.270 --> 00:46:32.060
<v Yousef Hammash>My daughter Illya was crying because her aunts are crying, my wife is crying, my mother is crying. [SIGHS] And then I found myself in this chaotic situation, trying to understand if it's the right option or not, if it's--
<v Yousef Hammash>我的女儿伊利亚在哭，因为她的阿姨在哭，我的妻子在哭，我的母亲在哭。[叹气] 然后我发现自己陷入了这种混乱的境地，试图弄明白这到底是不是正确的选择，如果它——

00:46:32.060 --> 00:46:36.560
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>You were having doubts?
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>你有疑问吗？

00:46:36.560 --> 00:46:59.360
<v Yousef Hammash>Yeah, yeah, of course. I am going for nowhere, leaving behind me everything. An entire life. And this is the second time I'm leaving things behind. I left my house in the north toward the south. I left my house, my memories, everything in the north.
<v Yousef Hammash>是的，是的，当然。我要去一个未知的地方，把一切抛在身后。一整个人生。这是我第二次把东西抛在身后。我从北部的家搬向南部。我离开了我的家、我的回忆，北部的一切。

00:46:59.360 --> 00:47:14.840
<v Yousef Hammash>Now I'm trying to understand or to imagine how my sisters are feeling when they are losing their backup, their support. Whenever they want anything, whenever they are facing anything, they know that Yousef is there.
<v Yousef Hammash>现在我试图理解或想象我的姐妹们在失去依靠、失去支持时是什么感觉。无论她们想要什么，无论她们面临什么，她们都知道尤瑟夫在那里。

00:47:14.840 --> 00:47:20.260
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>What did they say, Yousef? What did they say to you?
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>她们说了什么，尤瑟夫？她们对你说了什么？

00:47:20.260 --> 00:47:41.240
<v Yousef Hammash>Everyone was in a shock, including me. Everyone was crying, and I was looking to my sisters. I felt how weak I am to make that decision. I don't have enough courage to leave everything behind. And this is one of the hardest moments in my life.
<v Yousef Hammash>每个人都震惊了，包括我。每个人都在哭，我看着我的姐妹们。我感到做出那个决定我是多么软弱。我没有足够的勇气把一切抛在身后。这是我一生中最困难的时刻之一。

00:47:41.240 --> 00:47:46.360
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Yeah.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>是的。

00:47:46.360 --> 00:48:10.720
<v Yousef Hammash>Yeah, it is [INAUDIBLE]. When I was looking for my sisters, when they are thinking about losing their entire family, it's not only me. It's my wife, my children, their mother. I couldn't find the right word. What should I say?
<v Yousef Hammash>是的，这是。[听不清] 当我看着我的姐妹们，想到她们要失去整个家庭，不仅是我，还有我的妻子、我的孩子、她们的母亲。我找不到合适的词。我该说什么？

00:48:10.720 --> 00:48:41.510
<v Yousef Hammash>And the issue is that I was very overwhelmed emotionally. And if I said-- and it happened. When I start to talk to them, I was trying to show how strong I am. And I was like, it's fine. Since a month I informed you to be prepared for this moment. Then here where I lost control of my emotions.
<v Yousef Hammash>问题是我的情绪完全崩溃了。如果我说——它就这样发生了。当我开始和她们说话时，我试图表现得坚强。我说，没事的。一个月前我就通知你们要为这一刻做好准备了。然后，就在这里，我失去了对情绪的控制。

00:48:41.510 --> 00:49:18.270
<v Yousef Hammash>It's usually I'm that tough man who cannot be seen as a weak person. And I understood how weak I am. And I don't want to be shown weak in front of them, but it's out of my hand. My sisters, I think they-- I believe they know. They know that I will do anything for them and whenever they need anything. I already prepared everything. And--
<v Yousef Hammash>通常我是那个不能表现得软弱的硬汉。我理解自己是多么软弱。我不想在她们面前表现得软弱，但我控制不住。我的姐妹们，我想她们……我相信她们知道。她们知道我会为她们做任何事，无论何时她们需要什么。我已经准备好了一切。而且——

00:49:18.270 --> 00:49:38.380
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Yousef, you told me over the last months that every time I asked how you feel about leaving, you were sort of like, I can't. I don't know. I'll know when it happens. I don't know. I can't think about it. Do you feel like you're suddenly thinking about it now?
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>尤瑟夫，过去几个月你告诉我，每次我问你对离开有什么感觉时，你总是说，我不能。我不知道。等到了那一天我自然会知道。我不知道。我不能想它。你现在突然觉得自己在想它了吗？

00:49:38.380 --> 00:50:14.390
<v Yousef Hammash>I was postponing thinking about it because I understood how hard it is. And I was doing right. I was doing right today when I received the news and then knowing that I'm leaving tomorrow. I never felt the pain inside me like today. And I was right. I was right. And now it's real. It's happening. And I'm leaving Gaza tomorrow. It's like losing my identity.
<v Yousef Hammash>我一直在推迟思考它，因为我明白这有多难。我这样做是对的。我今天收到消息知道明天要离开时，我确实做到了。我从未像今天这样感到内心的痛苦。我是对的。我是对的。现在一切成真了。它正在发生。我明天就要离开加沙了。这就像失去了我的身份。

00:50:14.390 --> 00:50:15.770
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>When are you leaving?
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>你什么时候走？

00:50:15.770 --> 00:50:17.420
<v Yousef Hammash>I'm leaving 7:00 AM in the morning.
<v Yousef Hammash>我明天早上7点出发。

00:50:17.420 --> 00:50:22.940
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Oh, wow. You're leaving in six hours.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>哦，哇。六个小时后你就要走了。

00:50:22.940 --> 00:50:28.070
<v Yousef Hammash>Yeah, I'm leaving.
<v Yousef Hammash>是的，我要走了。

00:50:28.070 --> 00:50:32.690
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Are you going to sleep?
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>你能睡着吗？

00:50:32.690 --> 00:51:00.870
<v Yousef Hammash>I don't know if I could manage to sleep. Because tomorrow morning, at 7:00 AM, I have to go to meet my sisters again before we leave. And I want to make sure, even if I have one more minute to spend it with them, I'll do it. I don't know. Chana, I'm going through one of the most difficult-- it's not one of the most. It's the most difficult decision I've made in my entire life.
<v Yousef Hammash>我不知道能不能睡着。因为明天早上7点，在我离开前我必须再去见我的姐妹们。即使还有一分钟的时间可以和她们在一起，我也会去做。我不知道。查娜，我正在经历我一生中最困难的——不，不是之一。这是我一生中做过的最困难的决定。

00:51:00.870 --> 00:51:04.140
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>I know.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>我知道。

00:51:04.140 --> 00:51:21.090
<v Yousef Hammash>And now I'm just leaving everything. Now I am leaving. And they will be refugee once again. Born as a refugee, raised as a refugee, and now starting a new life as a refugee.
<v Yousef Hammash>现在我把一切都留下了。现在我要走了。她们将再次成为难民。生为难民，长为难民，现在又开始了作为难民的新生活。

00:51:21.090 --> 00:51:30.690
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Yousef, I want to let you go have time with your family and also hopefully sleep some before you have to make that trip tomorrow.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>尤瑟夫，我想让你有时间和家人在一起，也希望你在明天出发前能睡一会儿。

00:51:30.690 --> 00:51:39.870
<v Yousef Hammash>Thanks. Thank you, Chana. Thank you so much. Yeah. Thank you. Thank you. And I think our next call will be from a different place.
<v Yousef Hammash>谢谢。谢谢你，查娜。非常感谢。是的。谢谢。谢谢。我想我们的下一次通话将会在不同的地方。

00:51:39.870 --> 00:51:41.920
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Yeah.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>是的。

00:51:41.920 --> 00:51:44.200
<v Yousef Hammash>Hopefully it will go OK.
<v Yousef Hammash>希望一切顺利。

00:51:44.200 --> 00:51:45.910
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>All right. Bye, Yousef.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>好的，再见，尤瑟夫。

00:51:45.910 --> 00:51:47.370
<v Yousef Hammash>Bye-bye. Bye-bye.
<v Yousef Hammash>再见。再见。

00:51:47.370 --> 00:51:59.250
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Bye.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>再见。

00:51:59.250 --> 00:52:28.350
<v Ira Glass>Yousef left through the Rafah crossing the next day. That day, his family saw the world outside Gaza for the first time. The kids were amazed by the electricity in Cairo and the trees. Trees in Gaza have been cut down now to use for fire. When Illya and Ahmed started to tell their cousins in Gaza about the watermelon they were eating and the playground they played on, Yousef had to tell them to keep that kind of thing to themselves from now on.
<v Ira Glass>尤瑟夫第二天穿过了拉法口岸。那天，他的家人第一次看到了加沙以外的世界。孩子们对开罗的电力和树木感到惊奇。加沙的树木现在都已被砍伐用作柴火。当伊利亚和艾哈迈德开始向加沙的表亲们讲述他们吃的西瓜和玩的游乐场时，尤瑟夫不得不告诉他们，从今往后要把这些事藏在心里。

00:52:28.350 --> 00:52:54.670
<v Ira Glass>Manal took the children to the market and bought chocolate. Yousef sat at the computer, continuing to try to make plans for his sisters, trying to figure out where were the Israeli tanks now, what might their approach into Rafah be, what was the intensity of the bombing that day, and what did it mean. Were the NGOs leaving Rafah yet? Were other people leaving? Was it time for his sisters to move somewhere else in Gaza?
<v Ira Glass>马纳尔带孩子们去市场买了巧克力。尤瑟夫坐在电脑前，继续努力为他的姐妹们做计划，试图弄清楚以色列坦克现在在哪儿，他们对拉法的进攻可能是什么方式，那天的轰炸强度如何，这意味着什么。非政府组织离开拉法了吗？其他人也离开了吗？是时候让他的姐妹们转移到加沙其他地方了吗？

00:52:54.670 --> 00:53:13.600
<v Ira Glass>Then, on May 6, the Israeli military sent tanks into Rafah. The invasion had finally started. That same day, there was news that Hamas had agreed to a ceasefire. It was very confusing, but for a couple hours, it seemed like maybe there was going to be a ceasefire.
<v Ira Glass>然后，在5月6日，以色列军队将坦克开进了拉法。入侵终于开始了。同一天，有消息称哈马斯同意了停火。情况非常混乱，但有那么几个小时，似乎好像真的要停火了。

00:53:13.600 --> 00:53:28.210
<v Yousef Hammash>I was very, very excited and hyped. And it was like, what to do? It's like, OK. Yaani, start to think about what next, what I'm going to do with the family. It's like, ah, I should go back to Gaza. And then I start even to look at what is the process to go back to Gaza as soon as I can. And--
<v Yousef Hammash>我非常、非常兴奋和激动。心想该怎么办？就像，好吧。就是说，开始思考下一步，我该怎么安排家人。我想，啊，我应该回到加沙。甚至我开始研究我能以多快速度回到加沙。然后——

00:53:28.210 --> 00:53:29.980
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>What? Really?
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>什么？真的吗？

00:53:29.980 --> 00:53:49.710
<v Yousef Hammash>It might take one, two weeks. Yeah. I'm useless here. What am I doing here? Watching the news? Writing reports? I want to be there. The only option for me is to go back to Gaza. And even with my sisters, I can just drop them in the car, and we keep running in Gaza from a place to the other. I don't mind it.
<v Yousef Hammash>可能需要一两周。是的。我在这里没用。我在这里做什么？看新闻？写报告？我想去那里。对我来说唯一的选择就是回到加沙。即使和我的姐妹们在一起，我也可以把她们接上车，我们继续在加沙从一个地方跑到另一个地方。我不介意。

00:53:49.710 --> 00:53:59.150
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Yousef was suddenly back to the person I remembered talking to for every other move before this last one-- energized, frantic.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>尤瑟夫突然又变回了我在之前每一次搬迁前认识的那个尤瑟夫——精力充沛、近乎疯狂。

00:53:59.150 --> 00:54:11.340
<v Yousef Hammash>I start to think rationally about what I'm going to happen, what I'm going to do. And the plan that I'm having now is to figure out a way how to come back.
<v Yousef Hammash>我开始理性地思考接下来会发生什么，我该做什么。我现在拥有的计划是找出回去的方法。

00:54:11.340 --> 00:54:38.220
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>But that day, there was no ceasefire. And the next day, the Israeli military seized the Rafah crossing into Egypt and closed the border. There was no way back. Yousef would be in one world. His sisters would be back home in another.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>但那一天，并没有停火。第二天，以色列军队占领了通往埃及的拉法口岸并关闭了边境。没有退路了。尤瑟夫将身处一个世界。他的姐妹们将回到家园，身处另一个世界。

00:54:38.220 --> 00:55:01.870
<v Ira Glass>Chana Joffe-Walt is one of the producers of our show. Chana's story about Yousef was edited by Laura Starecheski and Nancy Updike. Our episode today was produced by Aviva DeKornfeld. The people who put together today's episode include Jendayi Bonds, Zoe Chace, Michael Comite, Emmanuel Dzotsi, Katherine Rae Mondo, Nadia Reiman, Safiyah Riddle, Ryan Rumery, Frances Swanson, Christopher Swetala, Matt Tierney, Julie Whitaker, and Diane Wu.
<v Ira Glass>查娜·乔夫-沃尔特是我们节目的制片人之一。关于尤瑟夫的故事由劳拉·斯塔雷切斯基（Laura Starecheski）和南希·厄普代克（Nancy Updike）编辑。今天的一集由阿维娃·德科恩菲尔德（Aviva DeKornfeld）制作。参与今天制作的人员包括詹达伊·邦兹（Jendayi Bonds）、佐伊·蔡斯（Zoe Chace）、迈克尔·科米特（Michael Comite）、伊曼纽尔·佐齐（Emmanuel Dzotsi）、凯瑟琳·雷·蒙多（Katherine Rae Mondo）、娜迪亚·雷曼（Nadia Reiman）、萨菲娅·里德尔（Safiyah Riddle）、瑞安·鲁梅里（Ryan Rumery）、弗朗西丝·斯旺森（Frances Swanson）、克里斯托弗·斯韦塔拉（Christopher Swetala）、马特·蒂尔尼（Matt Tierney）、朱莉·惠特克（Julie Whitaker）和黛安·吴（Diane Wu）。

00:55:01.870 --> 00:55:21.090
<v Ira Glass>Our managing editor is Sarah Abdurrahman. Our senior editor is David Kestenbaum. Our executive editor is Emanuele Berry. Reporting, research, and Arabic translation from Hany Hawasly. Arabic interpreting from Emna Zghal and Sawsan Abdelatif. Arabic voiceover by Leem Lubany. Additional reporting by Fatma and by Dana Ballout.
<v Ira Glass>我们的执行编辑是萨拉·阿卜杜勒拉赫曼（Sarah Abdurrahman）。我们的资深编辑是戴维·凯斯滕鲍姆（David Kestenbaum）。我们的总编辑是埃曼纽尔·贝里（Emanuele Berry）。报道、研究和阿拉伯语翻译来自哈尼·哈瓦斯利（Hany Hawasly）。阿拉伯语口译来自埃姆娜·兹加尔（Emna Zghal）和索桑·阿卜杜勒拉蒂夫（Sawsan Abdelatif）。阿拉伯语配音来自利姆·卢巴尼（Leem Lubany）。额外报道由法特玛（Fatma）和达娜·巴鲁特（Dana Ballout）提供。

00:55:21.090 --> 00:55:34.380
